shoprouter-rl
=============

A COMPOSITE agent: a public production backbone + an original RL-trained selling head.

PRODUCTION BACKBONE (third-party, Apache-2.0)
  Author  : yhay81 (Yusuke Hayashi)
  Source  : Kaggle kernel `yhay81/three-day-shop-router`  (agent hybrid_shopforge_3day_frontier_state_router_r5)
  Files   : _shop_bridge.py (its ctypes bridge, renamed), agent.so (compiled in Kaggle's runtime,
            GLIBC <= 2.14), source/ (its C++ sources, SPDX Apache-2.0 headers).
  Used unchanged, under the Apache License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

MARKET-DENIAL HEAD (our original work)
  An additive selling policy (main.py `_head_sells`) that appends extra non-wheat SELLs in leftover
  market slots. Parameters (_W, _BIAS) were trained by Evolution Strategies against a mixed opponent
  panel (shoprouter/tfuku/starter), optimizing the terminal-margin DELTA over the raw backbone.
  Training harness: scratchpad rl_markethead/ (env.py, train_panel.py). This is NOT part of the
  upstream agent; it is our contribution and the reason this agent beats the raw backbone.

WHY IT'S A COMPOSITE, NOT A CLONE: the backbone's production/selling is a tightly-coupled whole
(replacing its selling collapses it), so the head is strictly ADDITIVE -- it never removes or alters
the backbone's own orders, only adds denial sells in spare slots. Measured vs the raw backbone:
+$3.2k head-to-head (8/8, two seed blocks); within +-$300 (noise) vs tfuku/top10/starter.

OUR CHANGE IN v2 -- PRICE-FLOOR SKIP
  The head no longer sells an item quoted below $3. A sale at the $1 floor yields $1 AND
  does not add market supply (`if (price > 1) inventory += 1` in the engine), so it
  neither earns nor denies -- the unit is strictly wasted, and the town drain re-prices
  it if held. Measured on 182 REAL ladder games (replay counterfactual, which reproduces
  official margins exactly for additive changes to the agent that played them):
      shipped shoprouter-rl : 130/182
      v2 (floor $3)         : 131/182   -- converts one loss, gives up zero wins
  Searched and rejected: floors at $10/$25 (no gain), $50 (-9 games), and per-item
  fertilizer/wool floors (no gain; a fertilizer floor CANCELS the $3 gain). Also
  ablated the head's item set -- no item should be dropped (strawberry is worth 11
  games, milk/wool/fertilizer 2 each).
